{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789210733,"nonce":"/RIXXTUzxu3lb4SSV4nGvweMaOs=","title":"AOT fast-path arity cap 8 sent 15-arg constructor to the empty-blocks MIR stub","message":"Fixed in commit 39f242f. Record migrated from session memory 2026-09-12.\n\n\n\n**Root cause**: The three AOT-stub fast paths in `call_closure_sync`,\n`call_closure_sync_no_recv`, and `call_constructor_sync_impl` all\ngated invocation on `args.len() \u003c= 8` (or 7 for no-receiver variant).\nFor high-arity methods like `GltfMaterial.new_` (15 args), the fast\npath was skipped. The slow path then hit the empty-blocks MIR stub\nand returned `live_instance` without invoking the AOT-compiled body —\nevery field stayed at the default uninitialised Value.\n\n**Fix**: Widen cap to 15 user args (16 total including receiver) in\nall three sites; bump `jit_args` buffers from `[Value::null(); 8]` to\n`[Value::null(); 16]` to match. `call_jit_fn`'s arity ladder already\nhas explicit arms 0..=16 so no further runtime work needed.\n\n**Verification**:\n- 923 lib tests pass (no regression)\n- 21/21 `aot_runtime` tests pass\n- Procedural-world AOT boots + runs render loop cleanly\n\n\n1. Plugin-side `eprintln!` in `wlift_gpu`'s `write_buffer_with` →\n   captured the failing list's bits + element values. Initial reading\n   suggested obj_type-byte flip; further inspection showed real Lists\n   of NULL values.\n2. Wren-side `System.print` at Material constructor entry +\n   exit: confirmed Material's ctor ran with correct fields BUT\n   the source values came from a null-fielded GltfMaterial.\n3. GltfMaterial constructor-entry print: NEVER FIRED for the\n   foliage instances → constructor never invoked.\n4. Cross-referenced arity (15) against the fast-path gate (≤8) →\n   bingo.\n\n\n\n`wlift --aot procedural-world_aot procedural-world.hatch` produces a binary that runs through GPU init, then crashes with:\n\n```\nError: Buffer.writeFloats: every element must be a number (index 0).\nError: Buffer.writeFloats: every element must be a number (index 0).\n```\n\nTiered + interpreter pass fine. Direct `wlift main.wren` (not bundled) passes.\nSingle-class minimal repros (Float32Array, instance fields, inheritance, cross-module) all PASS under AOT.\n\n\nInstrumented `plugins/wlift_gpu/src/lib.rs` to print `slot(3).bits`, obj_type,\ncount, and elements [0..4] on every writeFloats call. The first Material's\npackUniform_ writes a clean count=16 list with [0..3] = 1.0 (terrain\nmaterial's `_albedoColor = Vec4(1,1,1,1)` packed). The SECOND Material\nreuses the same `_matUboFloats` list address but every slot reads back\nas `0x7ffc_0000_0000_0000` — exact bits of `Value::NULL`.\n\n```\n[DBG] count=16 [0]=0x3ff0... [1]=0x3ff0... [2]=0x3ff0... [3]=0x3ff0...  ← terrain Material OK\n[DBG] count=16 [0]=0x7ffc... [1]=0x7ffc... [2]=0x7ffc... [3]=0x7ffc...  ← foliage Material — all NULLs\n[DBG] FAIL i=0 v.bits=0x7ffc... v.obj_type=None\n```\n\nBoth calls use the SAME list address (`_matUboFloats` reused). Between them,\n`_matUboFloats.clear()` + `material.packUniform_(_matUboFloats)` runs. The\nsecond material's `_albedoColor.x` (and every other field accessor inside\npackUniform_) adds null to the list — meaning the Material instance's\nfields read back as null.\n\n\nA Material instance constructed under AOT has its instance fields (the\n~16 `_albedoColor / _metallicFactor / _emissiveColor / _alphaMode / ...`\ndeclared in `gpu_material.wren:31-76`) come back as null when read AFTER\nthe first Material is constructed. Sibling Material instances either:\n- Share field-slot storage with the first Material (slot aliasing across instances of the SAME class — unusual)\n- Have their constructor body truncated mid-way under AOT lowering\n- Have fields read from the wrong instance offset\n\nThe triggering class shape: **Material has two constructors** (`new()` and\n`new(color)` — both setting the same 16 fields). The first Material in\nthe demo is built via `Material.new(Vec4.new(1,1,1,1))` for terrain. The\nsecond is built via @hatch:gltf when loading Quaternius gltf files —\nlikely via `Material.new()` (no args) followed by setter assignments.\n\n\n- Float32Array → List obj_type byte flip (refuted: real Lists with valid\n  Num data in first 4 writeFloats calls).\n- `_scratch.add(0)` miscompiling to null (refuted by minimal grow-list repro).\n- PostPass→Tonemap inheritance slot aliasing (refuted by minimal repro).\n- Cross-module Float32Array instance field load (refuted).\n- Foreign-call arg corruption (slot 3 is a stable List pointer; bug is\n  inside the List's element values).\n\n\nA 4-phase workflow tested the cross-package-class-layout theory and\nfalsified it via direct code reading:\n\n- **`scan_expr_fields` missing recursive Expr arms** — REFUTED. Every arm\n  with sub-expressions is covered at `src/mir/builder.rs:2148-2240`\n  (Closure, Interpolation, Subscript, Conditional, SubscriptSet,\n  ListLiteral, MapLiteral, Range, Is, CompoundAssign, UnaryOp,\n  BinaryOp, LogicalOp, Call, Assign, SuperCall). Bare `_ =\u003e {}`\n  catches only leaves.\n- **AOT `walk_hatch_archive` not threading `field_layouts`** — REFUTED.\n  Both `walk_imports` (`.wren` path, `src/codegen/aot.rs:198-221`) and\n  `walk_hatch_archive` (`.hatch` archive path, `src/codegen/aot.rs:436-446`)\n  thread the same `HashMap\u003cString, Vec\u003cString\u003e\u003e` through\n  `lower_module_with_known_classes` identically to the tiered fix at\n  `src/hatch.rs:1132-1244`.\n\n**Minimal repro at `/tmp/aot-mat-repro/`** (4-package workspace mirroring\nthe demo's shape: pkg_math V4 → pkg_a class A with 16 fields + two\nctors → pkg_b Loader/Mesh → repro/main.wren constructing two A\ninstances via setter chain) **cannot reproduce** the null-field bug.\nTested ingredients: cross-package inheritance, ctor overloads, setter\nchains, state-machine yield (`Fiber.yield(null)`), field-storage in a\n`_meshes` List. All variants pass under both tiered AND AOT.\n\n\nAdded `System.print` at the entry of both `Material.new()` and `new(color)`\nconstructors PLUS at the start of `packUniform_`. Captured this:\n\n```\n[DBG mat-ctor-1arg] entered color=Vec4   ← terrain Material\n[DBG mat-ctor-noarg] entered             ← foliage Material 1\n... (7 more foliage Material ctor entries)\n[DBG mat] this=Material _albedoColor=Vec4 _emissiveColor=Vec4 _metallicFactor=0 ... _sway=0 _revision=4  ← terrain packUniform_ ✅\n[DBG mat] this=Material _albedoColor=null _emissiveColor=null _metallicFactor=null ... _sway=0.85 _revision=10  ← foliage packUniform_ ❌\n```\n\n**The constructor body IS running** (\"entered\" prints). But reads later\nreturn null for every constructor-only-initialized field.\n\n**Key clue: `_sway=0.85` and `_revision=10` read correctly.** These are the\nONLY two fields mutated via SETTERS at runtime (the foliage_scene.wren\ncode does `material.sway = swayV`; the sway setter increments _revision).\n\nSetter writes persist. Constructor writes don't.\n\nAlso confirmed via `eprintln!` in `call_constructor_sync_impl`: for every\nMaterial allocation, `has_active_interp_frames=false`, so the JIT-ptr\nfast path IS being taken. The AOT-compiled constructor body IS being\ninvoked. But its writes to instance fields don't persist.\n\n\nInside Material.new()'s body: `_albedoColor = Vec4.new(1, 1, 1, 1)`.\nThe Vec4 allocation can trigger GC. If GC moves the instance (or the\ninstance pointer is held in a register that GC can't update), the\nsubsequent SetField `_albedoColor` writes to the STALE pointer. All\nsubsequent field writes follow.\n\nThis explains the pattern:\n- Terrain `Material.new(color)`: first field is `_albedoColor = color` (no alloc) → stable. Subsequent allocs hit when `this` happens to still be live, OR the codegen does the right thing only when there's a leading non-allocating write.\n- Foliage `Material.new()`: first field is `_albedoColor = Vec4.new(...)` (alloc immediately). Vec4 alloc GCs, `this` register goes stale, all writes lost.\n- Setters run AFTER the GC + after `this` is reloaded from the live instance pointer (returned from the constructor + stored in `m`). They write to the live instance.\n\nCompanion to `project_aot_subscript_forwarded_receiver.md` (commit\n`8f4267c`): SM-load fresh ValueIds needed stack-map root registration.\nSame class of bug, different code path.\n\n**Failed fix attempts this session:**\n- 49f6d02: empty-blocks guard in no-fiber arm of `call_constructor_sync` —\n  fixed a separate panic but didn't fix this null-fields bug.\n- `aot_only` override at vm.rs:5455 to force JIT-ptr usage when MIR is\n  empty regardless of `has_active_interp_frames` — irrelevant: the\n  `eprintln!` showed `has_active_interp_frames=false` for every Material\n  ctor, so the fast path was already being taken. My override was a no-op.\n\n\nThe remaining structural difference: terrain Material's field values are\nliteral Wren constants (`Vec4.new(1,1,1,1)`); foliage Material's field\nvalues originate inside `@hatch:gltf`'s GLB binary parser, cross the\n`wlift_abi` boundary, then feed into a Wren-side Material setter chain.\nThis matches the pattern of three prior AOT-only null-field bugs:\n\n- `project_aot_subscript_forwarded_receiver.md` — fixed by `8f4267c`\n  (SM-load fresh ValueIds declared as stack-map roots).\n- `project_aot_load_arg_wrong_frame.md` — fixed by `0611a6d`\n  (`wlift_aot_sm_load_arg` read `frames.last()` on resume).\n- `project_aot_gc_pass1_covered_fps.md` — fixed by `d8739d9`\n  (Pass-1 stack walker mistakenly marked fp covered before lookup).\n\nAll three were stack-map / boundary-marshaling miscompiles surfacing as\nnull fields on the AOT side only.\n\n\nBuild a minimal plugin shim that does what `@hatch:gltf` does:\n1. New crate `crates/wlift_aot_repro_plugin` (cdylib) that defines a\n   single foreign method returning a struct of ~16 Value fields.\n2. Wren-side wrapper class with two ctors that pull values from the\n   plugin call into instance fields.\n3. Build as .hatch, AOT-compile, construct two instances, print each\n   field.\n\nIf this reproduces the null-field bug, the next-step is to\ninstrument `crates/wlift_abi/src/` Value marshaling under AOT and\nlook for an SM-root miss around the `extern \"C\"` boundary.\n\nIf it doesn't reproduce, the GC-during-construction angle is the\nbackstop: loop A.new(...) thousands of times, force `Hatch.gc()`\nmid-loop, check field reads at random indices on instances stored\nbehind a deep root path (`_meshes` List inside a `Scene` field).\n\n\nUse tiered mode (`hatch run`). AOT is the blocker; tiered renders\ncorrectly + the demo is in good shape.\n\n\n- `project_postfx_inheritance_blocker.md` — class field slot aliasing\n  bug (parent-subclass), already documented.\n- `feedback_bare_var_branch_assign.md` — late-method local slot aliasing.\n- `ee01a4d` — wlift fix for cross-package class layouts (tiered only;\n  AOT may need the same fix at the AOT lowering layer).","files":null}]}